---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

export const prerender = true;

const title = "About | Pinto Injury Resources";
const description =
  "Pinto Injury Resources is an educational website created to help people better understand California personal injury insurance claim processes. Educational information only — not legal advice.";

const canonical = "https://pintoinjury.com/about/";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} />
  </head>

  <body>
    <Header />

    <main class="container" style="padding: 3rem 1rem;">
      <article style="max-width: 75ch;">
        <h1 style="font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          About Pinto Injury Resources
        </h1>

        <p style="font-size: 1.125rem; opacity: 0.92;">
          Pinto Injury Resources is an educational website created to help people better understand how personal injury insurance claims commonly work in California.
        </p>

        <p>
          After a car accident, many people quickly discover that the insurance process can feel confusing, stressful, and difficult to understand. Questions often arise about claim timelines, medical documentation, insurance investigations, settlement discussions, vehicle damage, and what typically happens as a claim moves through the process.
        </p>

        <p>
          The goal of this website is simple: to make that process easier to understand through clear, practical, plain-English educational content.
        </p>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Why this site exists</h2>

        <p>
          Many people involved in accidents are exposed to unfamiliar insurance procedures for the first time.
        </p>

        <p>
          Terms such as liability investigation, documentation review, recorded statements, medical records, settlement evaluation, claim delays, repair estimates, and comparative fault can quickly become overwhelming.
        </p>

        <p>
          Pinto Injury Resources was created to help explain these topics in a way that is easier to understand.
        </p>

        <p>
          The focus of this site is education, transparency, and helping readers better understand how accident-related insurance claims often develop over time.
        </p>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">What this website covers</h2>

        <p>
          This website publishes educational articles focused on topics commonly connected to California car accident claims, including:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>insurance claim timelines</li>
          <li>documentation and evidence review</li>
          <li>vehicle damage and repair issues</li>
          <li>accident investigations and fault disputes</li>
          <li>common insurance communication issues</li>
          <li>general accident claim processes in California</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          The content is intended to be practical, accessible, and easy to understand for people who simply want to learn more about how these systems commonly operate.
        </p>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Why understanding the process matters</h2>

        <p>
          For many people, the most difficult part of an accident claim is uncertainty.
        </p>

        <p>
          The insurance process often involves multiple stages happening behind the scenes, and delays or changing timelines can create confusion and frustration.
        </p>

        <p>
          Understanding how these systems commonly work can help people become more informed while learning about the general claim process.
        </p>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">About the author</h2>

        <p>
         This website is independently operated by a California law student with a long-term professional interest in personal injury law, insurance claim systems, and improving public understanding of how accident-related claims are commonly handled.

The purpose of this project is to study and explain complex legal and insurance-related topics in a way that is practical, accessible, and easier for everyday people to understand.

Over time, this website is intended to become a long-term educational resource focused on helping readers better understand accident-related insurance processes in California.</p>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Important notice</h2>

        <p>
          Pinto Injury Resources is <strong>not a law firm</strong> and does <strong>not</strong> provide legal advice, legal opinions, legal representation, or individualized guidance.
        </p>

        <p>
          The information provided on this website is intended solely for <strong>general educational purposes</strong>.
        </p>

        <p>
          Reading content on this website does <strong>not</strong> create an attorney-client relationship, and the information provided should not be relied upon as a substitute for advice from a licensed attorney who can evaluate specific individual circumstances.
        </p>

        <p>
          Laws, procedures, insurance practices, and claim outcomes vary depending on the facts of each situation.
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>